   132	
   133	    Input structure:
   134	    - A single main grid with one dominant background color, one solid teal (8) square, and 3-4 isolated colored obstacle pixels.
   135	    - There is no legend region, and every obstacle is exactly one cell large.
   136	
   137	    Rule:
   138	    - Launch one square-width teal beam in each cardinal direction from the teal square.
   139	    - A beam paints teal only onto background cells as its sz x sz footprint slides.
   140	    - If the next footprint would include an obstacle pixel at (r, c), do not advance into that step; instead compare row and column:
   141	      row > col means turn clockwise, row < col means turn counterclockwise.
   142	    - Continue from the current location after turning, and stop once the next step would leave the grid.
   143	
   144	    Key insight: The removed legend and vanished shape cue are both replaced by a positional code:
   145	    isolated pixels below the main diagonal force clockwise turns, while pixels above it force counterclockwise turns.
   146	    """
   147	    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
   148	    assert g.size, "input grid must be non-empty"
